<title>TURKEY: TURK FIRMS-FLUGHAFEN WIEN WIN AIRPORT PROJECT.</title>
<headline>TURK FIRMS-FLUGHAFEN WIEN WIN AIRPORT PROJECT.</headline>
<dateline>ISTANBUL 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>A consortium of Turkey's Tepe and Akfen firms and Austria's Flughafen Wien have won a $307 million project for the expansion of Istanbul's Ataturk airport, the Anatolian news agency said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>It said Tepe had 75 percent, Akfen 25 percent and Flughafen had five percent stake in the consortium which will build a new international flights terminal, a multi-storey car park and related facilities in 30 months.</p>
</text>
